  "result": "The option order in `--help` is fixed. Short options now come before long ones, so `-a, --alpha` and `-h, --help` display the way Click normally does.\n\n**Cause:** In `src/click/formatting.py`, `join_options()` sorted option names with `reverse=True`, which put `--long` before `-s`. I removed the `reverse=True` on line 319. The change is one line.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Sample commands now print `-a, --alpha TEXT`, `-m, --mid TEXT`, and `-h, --help`.\n- The full test suite passes: 1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed, 0 failed. Before the fix, the existing `tests/test_commands.py` expectation of `-h, --help` was already inconsistent with the output.\n\nI didn't commit the change. The working tree has one modified file, `src/click/formatting.py`.",
